Good morning from the Pompano Beach Daily! Here is what is happening around town this week. First, the city commission approved plans for the new beachfront boardwalk revitalization project, slated to begin next month. Second, local volunteers gathered at the community park this past Saturday for a successful coastal cleanup event, removing over five hundred pounds of debris. Third, the annual seafood festival has announced its headlining musical acts for the upcoming weekend celebration. Stay tuned for more local updates.
